  "Question": "The interval between the consecutive integers -2 and -1 on a number line is divided into 4 equal parts. What number is represented by the 1st division point to the right of -2?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "-1.75",
    "B": "-2.25",
    "C": "-1.5",
    "D": "-1.25"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Each small interval has length \\(1/4=0.25\\). Moving 1 interval to the right from -2 gives \\(-2+0.25=-1.75\\) (numbers increase as you move to the right).",
